Changes to configured tracked attributes are detected, and the current record is expired (end-dated and its current flag turned off) when a tracked attribute changes.
Unchanged records are not updated or duplicated — no new version is created when the tracked attributes are identical.
Previously expired historical versions remain unchanged.
Exactly one current record exists for each active business key after successful processing.
Reprocessing the same input is idempotent — running it again does not create duplicate historical versions.
